From ceb3d135a5ac4cf32897f6088c88632fb3dde4ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:55:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Dual-branch distillation, ln01 variant (0056 + 0057 rebased
 onto the patch-0051 launcher)

For the "cognitive map as a training-time modality" setting: at test time
the raster is zeroed (metadata kept, every module in place, i.e.
map_ablation metadata_only); at training time every step runs the policy
twice, with its LLM raster (map branch) and with the raster zeroed (zero
branch, the deployment view, same dropout masks by RNG replay, gradient on).

  L = CE(zero) + CE(map)
      + distill_weight * [ KL(T || map) + KL(T || zero) ]     (GT teacher)
      + dual_llm_weight * KL(sg[map] || zero)                 (map -> zero)

Stop-gradient on the map side of the last term: otherwise the cheapest
solution is for the map branch to stop reading its raster and collapse
onto the zero branch.  Rollout actions are sampled from the zero branch
(the deployed policy) by default, so DAgger's data distribution is the
deployed one; IL.dual_rollout_branch map switches that.  The two GT-KL
terms are separate switches (dual_gt_kl_on_map_branch /
dual_gt_kl_on_zero_branch), so the chain (GT -> map -> zero) and the
pure parallel form are ablations of the same code.

Exclusive with effect matching; the gate and the STOP factorisation apply
to both GT-KL terms if enabled (off by default).  IL.dual_enabled False
(default) leaves every existing path untouched.  Launcher mode dual with
DUAL_* / STOP_FACTORIZED pass-throughs.  Logs: student_ce (map branch),
student_ce_zero, self_kl, gt_kl_map, gt_kl_zero.  Tests: 3 (self-KL zero
when the branches agree, gradient only on the zero branch, config defaults).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CBCms1itAt1L2773SVd2gS
